`streamChatWithTools` calls `adapter.chat()` to probe for tool calls and then (when none) calls `adapter.streamChat()` again with the same options (including tools). This double-invokes the model, can produce a different answer than the probed `result`, increases cost/latency, and may allow tool-call events to appear during `streamChat` that will be forwarded to the client without being resolved by the loop. Consider redesigning so the streaming path is driven by `streamChat` events (handling tool-call/tool-call-delta), or at minimum avoid the second model call by streaming the already-returned `result` and/or disabling tools for the final streaming call.
```suggestion
        // Final round — return the probed result without an extra model call
        yield { type: 'text-delta', textDelta: result.content };
        yield { type: 'finish', result };
```

`POST /api/v1/ai/conversations` casts `req.body` to `Record<string, unknown>` and then unconditionally mutates it (`options.userId = ...`). If `req.body` is not an object (e.g. a string/number/array from a malformed client), this will throw before returning a 4xx. Add a type check similar to other handlers (ensure body is a non-null object) and return 400 on invalid payloads.
```suggestion
          // Ensure the request body is a non-null object before mutating it
          if (req.body === null || typeof req.body !== 'object' || Array.isArray(req.body)) {
            return { status: 400, body: { error: 'Invalid request payload' } };
          }

          const options: Record<string, unknown> = { ...(req.body as Record<string, unknown>) };

          // Bind the conversation to the authenticated user
          if (req.user?.userId) {
            options.userId = req.user.userId;
          }
```
